{"body":"The supported MIM release preserves unsupported scientific claims for further curation. SSSOM finalization in #731 completes the disposition review for all **3,018 mapping rows**: **1,763 supported** and **1,255 withheld**. The complete source graph remains semantically unapproved.\n\nCurrent mapping snapshot: [mim-sssom-2026-09-21](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/releases/tag/mim-sssom-2026-09-21). Its separate `withheld_mappings.sssom.tsv` preserves every withheld source row; `mapping-dispositions.tsv` records all 3,018 decisions, reasons and evidence references. Missing support does not necessarily establish that a claim is false. Non-exact mapping relations, weak exact-match evidence, unresolved aliases and identity conflicts remain withheld.\n\nThe trait-synonym source cleanup in #703 is now complete: 46 activity phrases across 39 records are retained as rejected provenance. The original negative #724 decision remains archived; the corrected Aromatic Compound row has a separate evidence-bound review. Adversarial review #730 fixes publication and integrity defects by source correction, precise withholding and regression checks. Closing #730 does not declare the withheld source claims scientifically corrected.\n\nThe [earlier KGX snapshot](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/releases/tag/mim-supported-2026-09-21) remains historical: 4,587 nodes, 2,112 edges, 1,603 mappings and 2,411 excluded assertions. The new SSSOM supersedes that snapshot's mapping selection; a corresponding new KGX publication is still pending. Current graph review ledgers account for 2,251 excluded assertions and preserve 1,735 open major/blocking historical findings. These counts overlap and are not additive.\n\nPriority evidence gaps in the current source corpus:\n\n- The 1,255 withheld mapping rows in the new lossless SSSOM backlog.\n- 662 prediction-only roles and 11 roles without evidence.\n- 24 additional unverified role promotions: generic mineral labels had become trace-element, iron, phosphate, or sulfur requirements, and a generic growth-factor label had become a vitamin claim. Review #720 records the affected assertions.\n- 43 component assertions requiring the original source preparation, including the unresolved PYGS abbreviation and TYGVS formulation differences.\n- The flattened CMC/PY/horse-serum expression remains AMBIGUOUS after withdrawal of its false single-mixture identity.\n- Other record-level findings remain explicit in the full disposition ledger.\n\nResolve each claim from its exact source identity, organism and preparation; add content-bound scientific dispositions and regenerate the affected artifacts. Do not bulk approve from chemical ancestry, name patterns, citation presence or structural validation. New evidence may move claims into the supported release only after review.\n\nSee [standalone SSSOM reproduction instructions](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/main/docs/SSSOM_RELEASE.md) and [mapping review evidence](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/tree/main/reports/sssom_completion_20260921). This issue remains open for scientific curation after #731.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABhn046A","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"The native reviewed export was regenerated and its source/review/partition hashes checked at MIM `4625afd492b6cf43e3b499d1425d2453d490009d`. Before the separately scoped melezitose correction, the current reproducible source contains **2,987 mapping rows: 1,741 supported and 1,246 withheld**, with withheld rows belonging to 1,001 owner records. The 3,018 / 1,763 / 1,255 numbers above describe the historical September release and should not be read as current corpus counts.\n\nI classified every existing withheld disposition by its recorded leading reason, retaining the full row selector, owner hash, reason and evidence reference. These are disjoint text-based inventory categories, not new scientific judgments:\n\n| Recorded leading reason | Rows |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Record-specific mapping, identity, alias or evidence concern | 548 |\n| Current non-exact relation and synonym scope not established | 202 |\n| Complete synonym payload lacks individual same-subject documentation | 196 |\n| Individual reasons outside those standard prefixes, preserved verbatim | 96 |\n| Cross-record baseline remains an unresolved review obligation | 56 |\n| Preparation/concentration/instruction tokens need same-subject review | 49 |\n| Label-index different-substance chemistry conflict | 39 |\n| Lexical or close grounding does not establish exact equivalence | 35 |\n| Changed/new row or owner no longer bound by the prior review | 20 |\n| No mapping-specific positive disposition | 5 |\n\nThe withheld predicates are **997 exactMatch, 152 broadMatch and 97 closeMatch**. All 1,741 supported rows are exactMatch. A recorded reason can contain several concerns; the full text, rather than the leading-reason category, governs follow-up. A withheld row is not automatically a false assertion.\n\nThis is a mapping-only, deterministic inventory (`scientific_review: false`). It does not approve roles, components, the complete source graph, or downstream media; it does not reassess the other historical counts in the issue body. The exact snapshot and classification rules are saved under `output/sssom-curation-20261101T003435Z/audit718/baseline/`, including native manifest, disposition and evidence bytes and SHA-256 hashes.\n\nThe stale counts in `docs/SSSOM_RELEASE.md` will be refreshed against the final verified native export after this batch's content-bound mapping receipts are assembled. That document update will distinguish the historical published release from the reproducible current export. No blanket scientific approval or disposition change is part of this documentation correction; this issue remains open.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-01T00:43:31Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/718#issuecomment-6551320808","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABhoAozA","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"[PR #1007](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1007) records the reproduced current release: 2,987 canonical rows, 1,740 supported and 1,247 withheld across 1,001 owners. Nine rows change, no rows are added/deleted/repositioned, and the carnitine registry approval is withdrawn after its owner changes. Native semantic integrity passes; full scientific release remains FAIL with 1,733 findings/2,272 assertions. The complete withheld-row/reason inventory and corrected guide are included. The raw 2,980-row generator output is not promoted wholesale because it changes 2,364 payloads, removes ten rows and adds three. [Evidence and native reviews](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/bf7d514c804670ea3db3e9e75a2c94624554fa26/reports/sssom_scientific_curation_20261101/README.md). This issue remains open; structural checks do not approve the backlog.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-01T01:02:44Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/718#issuecomment-6551513292","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkGcHwg","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Worker 01 continuation separates established source identities with concrete proposals from precise unresolved chemistry and source-version conflicts. Existing source snapshots and inherited holds remain preserved; a pending integration step is not itself missing scientific evidence.\n\n| Scope | Finding and disposition |\n| --- | --- |\n| PIPES, case 118 | CHEBI:39033 is a grouping term; the final 10 mM source label does not select the supplied neutral/salt form. Retain the scoped form requirement. The separate native author and independent PIPES reviews preserve this concern; #868 concerns different records. |\n| JCM 976 stock, KG case 170 | JCM 978 explicitly references JCM 976, not DSMZ 976. The complete stock is now an isolated existing-owner proposal, including every listed precursor, variable KOH to pH 6, literal preparation-water quantities and non-resolving ambiguous cross-reference labels. |\n| DSMZ 863 carbonate stock, KG case 186 | A distinct source-qualified owner proposal preserves 106 g Na2CO3 plus 1 L degassed water and sealed CO2 autoclaving. The current broadly shared CHEBI:29377 owner and its mixed dry/buffer aliases are untouched; they retain their separate whole-owner review obligations. |\n| Selenate forms, KG case 167 and root cases 14/42 | Explicit decahydrate in DSMZ 1493/1685 has a distinct CAS 10102-23-5 proposal with CHEBI:77775 as broad parent. TOGO M3118 prints Na2SeO4·5H2O, but Frolov's author-institution thesis p. 52 prints Na2SeO4 without hydrate at 94 mg/L trace stock (p. 53 dose 1 mL/L). That version conflict remains explicit; the thesis is not the exact publisher article. ATCC 2133/TOGO M2657 prints Na2SeO4·6H2O at 26 mg/L. Do not silently substitute selenite or anhydrous forms. |\n| Original selenium formulas, KG cases 169/187 | DSMZ 863 itself prints Na2Se2O3; DSMZ 973 itself prints Na2Se3·5H2O. Neither verifies the proposed familiar selenite spelling. Preserve literal source formulas pending authoritative reagent/formula clarification. |\n| Rubradirin, KG cases 179/181 | Unsuffixed source rubradirin does not establish RubradirinB. This concern is inherited from closed #752; do not reopen the already completed process-alias cleanup as a new defect. |\n| EBIOS, KG case 172 | JCM 969's Asahi dried-yeast tablets now have a product-specific registry proposal. Current tablet information is not backdated to a historical lot and does not identify EBIOS P2G yeast extract. |\n| Selenite/tungstate stock 431, cases 0/1/137/144 | Recovered source identity and decomposition now support the guarded registry/component proposal. The old generic composition hold is superseded for that exact scope; unrelated components, roles and release claims are not automatically approved. |\n\nThe following original-collection ambiguities stay in this MIM source-followup tracker rather than being assigned as KG-Microbe source-maintenance defects:\n\n| Original source and case | Specific clarification needed |\n| --- | --- |\n| DSMZ 1783 Solution 2, concentration case 122 | K2HPO4 amount 15.30 has no unit in the API and original PDF. Obtain the missing unit; do not assume grams. |\n| JCM 1419, concentration case 145 | Literal `0.1 M M FeCl2 solution` contains a duplicated concentration token. Preserve it until an authoritative correction. |\n| JCM 1462 and inherited 1463/1464 Ni/Se/W, named cases 71/111 | Printed `Na2WO2·2H2O`, 0.4 mg in a preparation listing 1 L added distilled water, requires an authoritative formula correction before exact tungstate grounding. |\n| DSMZ 436 Mineral solution 2, named case 129 | Both PDF/API print `CaCl2·7H2O` and percentages without a basis. Clarify the hydrate and percent basis; neither is an established API-only typo. |\n| CCAP S77, root case 146 | Original prints `NaSiO3·5H2O`,0.10 g. Restoring subscripts in the frozen instruction fragment does not establish disodium metasilicate. |\n| JCM 1430, root case 82 | Original itself prints `Distilled waterv`; the source spelling defect is distinct from the frozen L-to-mL error tracked with CultureMech. |\n\nThe borax hydration discrepancy is detailed in [#318](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/318), including the source-supported CHEBI:38888 owner proposal and separate stock exception. Source-defined products, water grades and complete stock formulations are supplied as isolated proposals instead of being left unresolved solely for integration.\n\nThe parenthetical labels on `84_GL_NaHCO3_Solution` are already non-resolving under current native text policy. Closed [#606](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/606) and [#610](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/610) cover that behavior. Optional REJECTED_LABEL typing changes no present resolver/export behavior and is not a new defect or a release fix.\n\nExact case IDs, frozen count definitions, source captures and proposal hashes: [KG26 decisions](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/root_substances/kg26/decisions.fragment.json), [concentration decisions](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/concentration_stocks/decisions.fragment.json), [named-stock source findings](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/named_stocks/issues-for-root.json) and [root-substance decisions](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/root_substances/decisions.fragment.json). No source chemistry, maintained MIM record or publication hold was changed by this evidence-lane work. The [final independent scientific review](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/final-188-scientific-review-v1.json) confirms the source-case outcomes and exact isolated proposals with their stated limits. Coordinator verification and future maintained integration remain separate.\n\nThe JCM 151 stock formulation is recovered, but its current MIM ownership is conflicted: UNMAPPED_0553 imports MediaDive 1883; `Trace_Mineral_Solution.yaml` imports MediaDive 897 and combines 151/852 aliases; `4-vinylphenol.yaml` carries incompatible trace-mineral aliases. JCM 265 uses a 1 L aliquot of the prepared JCM 151 stock, not necessarily the complete batch made with 1 L water. The proposed parent preserves that nested stock without a guessed catalog reference or duplicate owner. Reconcile the imported source identities and exact alias scopes using the [full owner records and hashes](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/named_stocks/quantity-v4/jcm151-owner-conflict.json). Closed [#861](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/861) explicitly left this source-specific identity question open while correcting review certainty; [#587](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/587) covers different instruction-form suggestions.\n\nFor case 14, the TOGO recipe lists 94 mg reagent plus 1000 mL added water. Only the thesis table explicitly supplies a 94 mg/L concentration basis. The two recipe versions and their different hydration claims remain separate.\n\n<!-- mim-review-round: all-unmatched-20261107-worker01-continuation; mim-fingerprints: w01-continuation-mediaingredientmech-718 -->\n","createdAt":"2026-11-08T05:16:52Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/718#issuecomment-6717638594","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":718,"state":"OPEN","title":"Curate the claims excluded from the reviewed MIM release","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/718"}
